{#
    A member's face, or their initials when they have none.

    One macro rather than an `<img>` pasted into the top bar, the member list
    and the payer field, for the same reason `partials/logo.twig` exists: the
    fallback is the part that gets forgotten, and a member with no picture
    should show two letters rather than a broken image.

    The initials form costs no request and follows the theme. It is also the
    accessible one by default — like the logo mark, both forms are decorative,
    because the member's name is always rendered beside the avatar and is what
    identifies them. Announcing "Sam" twice is worse than announcing it once.

    `id`          the member's user id; the picture is fetched from /avatars/{id}
    `name`        their display name, used only for the initials fallback
    `initials`    the letters to draw when there is no picture
    `has_avatar`  whether to try the picture at all
    `size`        the box to draw it in, in pixels

    The route answers 404 for a member of another household, which is why the
    caller passes `has_avatar` rather than this asking: a broken image is worse
    than initials, and the page already knows the answer.

    The size arrives as a custom property rather than a width class, because
    the two forms have to agree on it — an image sized by attributes and a
    circle of text sized by a class drift the moment either changes.
#}
{% macro face(id, name, initials, has_avatar, size = 32) %}
    {%- if has_avatar -%}
        <img class="avatar" src="/avatars/{{ id }}" alt=""
             width="{{ size }}" height="{{ size }}" loading="lazy"
             style="--avatar-size: {{ size }}px">
    {%- else -%}
        <span class="avatar avatar-initials" aria-hidden="true"
              style="--avatar-size: {{ size }}px">{{ initials }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}
